opt_eqrisk_lots -- equal option-risk lot sizing at the baseline premium outlay
metric: harness METRIC = 'opt' (option net, modelled); futures net shown for reference at the NEW lots

Deviations:
  - Real-set lot fallback for symbols absent from the known set (no known lot on any date): the rule has no case for this; lot = o_qty (treated as one lot), the rule's own fallback for an unverifiable lot.
  - Harness run() always recomputes 'fut' from net_<pol>; to show futures at the new lots in the harness 'futures' column, the trade function returns a copy whose net_<pol> = net_<pol> * L / fut_lots (the original column in D is untouched).

